Author: Oleg Nesterov <oleg-H+wXaHxf7aLQT0dZR+AlfA@public.gmane.org>
Date:   Wed Aug 26 14:29:24 2009 -0700

    clone(): fix race between copy_process() and de_thread()
   =20
    Spotted by Hiroshi Shimamoto who also provided the test-case below.
   =20
    copy_process() uses signal->count as a reference counter, but it is n=
ot.
    This test case
   =20
    	#include <sys/types.h>
    	#include <sys/wait.h>
    	#include <unistd.h>
    	#include <stdio.h>
    	#include <errno.h>
    	#include <pthread.h>
   =20
    	void *null_thread(void *p)
    	{
    		for (;;)
    			sleep(1);
   =20
    		return NULL;
    	}
   =20
    	void *exec_thread(void *p)
    	{
    		execl("/bin/true", "/bin/true", NULL);
   =20
    		return null_thread(p);
    	}
   =20
    	int main(int argc, char **argv)
    	{
    		for (;;) {
    			pid_t pid;
    			int ret, status;
   =20
    			pid =3D fork();
    			if (pid < 0)
    				break;
   =20
    			if (!pid) {
    				pthread_t tid;
   =20
    				pthread_create(&tid, NULL, exec_thread, NULL);
    				for (;;)
    					pthread_create(&tid, NULL, null_thread, NULL);
    			}
   =20
    			do {
    				ret =3D waitpid(pid, &status, 0);
    			} while (ret =3D=3D -1 && errno =3D=3D EINTR);
    		}
   =20
    		return 0;
    	}
   =20
    quickly creates an unkillable task.
   =20
    If copy_process(CLONE_THREAD) races with de_thread()
    copy_signal()->atomic(signal->count) breaks the signal->notify_count
    logic, and the execing thread can hang forever in kernel space.
   =20
    Change copy_process() to increment count/live only when we know for s=
ure
    we can't fail.  In this case the forked thread will take care of its
    reference to signal correctly.
   =20
    If copy_process() fails, check CLONE_THREAD flag.  If it it set - do
    nothing, the counters were not changed and current belongs to the sam=
e
    thread group.  If it is not set, ->signal must be released in any cas=
e
    (and ->count must be =3D=3D 1), the forked child is the only thread i=
n the
    thread group.
   =20
    We need more cleanups here, in particular signal->count should not be=
 used
    by de_thread/__exit_signal at all.  This patch only fixes the bug.
   =20
