    mm: fix for infinite churning of mlocked pages
   =20
    An mlocked page might lose the isolatation race.  This causes the pag=
e to
    clear PG_mlocked while it remains in a VM_LOCKED vma.  This means it =
can
    be put onto the [in]active list.  We can rescue it by using try_to_un=
map()
    in shrink_page_list().
   =20
    But now, As Wu Fengguang pointed out, vmscan has a bug.  If the page =
has
    PG_referenced, it can't reach try_to_unmap() in shrink_page_list() bu=
t is
    put into the active list.  If the page is referenced repeatedly, it c=
an
    remain on the [in]active list without being moving to the unevictable
    list.
   =20
    This patch fixes it.
   =20
