    V4L/DVB (12429): v4l2-ioctl: fix G_STD and G_PARM default handlers
   =20
    The v4l core supplies default handlers for G_STD and G_PARM. However,=
 both
    default handlers are buggy.
   =20
    This patch fixes the following:
   =20
    1) If no g_std is supplied and current_norm =3D=3D 0, then this drive=
r does not
       support TV video standards (e.g. a radio or webcam driver). Return
       -EINVAL. This ensures that there is no bogus VIDIOC_G_STD support =
for
       such drivers.
   =20
    2) The default VIDIOC_G_PARM handler used current_norm instead of fir=
st
       checking if the driver supported g_std and calling that to get the=
 norm.
       It also didn't check if current_norm was 0, since in that case the=
 driver
       does not support TV standards (or no standard was set at all) and =
the
       default handler should return -EINVAL.
   =20
    Note that I am very unhappy with these default handlers: I think they
    basically behave like some very strange and unexpected side-effect.
   =20
