    arch/ia64/Makefile: Remove -mtune=3Dmerced in IA64 kernel build
   =20
    Between GCC version 3.4.0 and 4.3.3 (including 3.4.0 and 4.3.3), -mtu=
ne=3Dmerced
    is implemented in GCC. Starting from 4.4.0, -mtune=3Dmerced is deprec=
ated.
   =20
    Even implemented in versions between 3.4.0 and 4.3.3, the -mtune=3Dme=
rced
    feature has been broken in some of the versions. For example, GCC 4.1=
.2 reports
    interanl tuning function errors during kernel building with -mtune=3D=
merced. Or
    GCC Bugzilla 16130 reports another -mtune=3Dmerced issue on GCC 3.4.1.
   =20
    So I would remove the -mtune=3Dmerced from IA64 kernel build. Without=
 this option,
    kernel on Merced will remain the same except losing an unstable and o=
ut-of-date
    performance tunning feature.
   =20
    Since GCC version 3.4.0, -mtune=3Dmckinley has been implemented. The
    -mtune=3Dmckinley option functions the same as mtune=3Ditanium2. And =
mtune=3Ditanium2
    is the default option. So we don't need to add mtune=3Dmckinley eithe=
r since its
    been the default option in any GCC version which implements this opti=
on.
   =20
    Signed-off-by: Fenghua Yu <fenghua.yu-ral2JQCrhuEAvxtiuMwx3w@public.gmane.org>

