Date:   Thu Aug 6 15:07:33 2009 -0700

    mm: make set_mempolicy(MPOL_INTERLEAV) N_HIGH_MEMORY aware
   =20
    At first, init_task's mems_allowed is initialized as this.
     init_task->mems_allowed =3D=3D node_state[N_POSSIBLE]
   =20
    And cpuset's top_cpuset mask is initialized as this
     top_cpuset->mems_allowed =3D node_state[N_HIGH_MEMORY]
   =20
    Before 2.6.29:
    policy's mems_allowed is initialized as this.
   =20
      1. update tasks->mems_allowed by its cpuset->mems_allowed.
      2. policy->mems_allowed =3D nodes_and(tasks->mems_allowed, user's m=
ask)
   =20
    Updating task's mems_allowed in reference to top_cpuset's one.
    cpuset's mems_allowed is aware of N_HIGH_MEMORY, always.
   =20
    In 2.6.30: After commit 58568d2a8215cb6f55caf2332017d7bdff954e1c
    ("cpuset,mm: update tasks' mems_allowed in time"), policy's mems_allo=
wed
    is initialized as this.
   =20
      1. policy->mems_allowd =3D nodes_and(task->mems_allowed, user's mas=
k)
   =20
    Here, if task is in top_cpuset, task->mems_allowed is not updated fro=
m
    init's one.  Assume user excutes command as #numactrl --interleave=3D=
all
    ,....
   =20
      policy->mems_allowd =3D nodes_and(N_POSSIBLE, ALL_SET_MASK)
   =20
    Then, policy's mems_allowd can includes a possible node, which has no=
 pgdat.
   =20
    MPOL's INTERLEAVE just scans nodemask of task->mems_allowd and access=
 this
    directly.
   =20
      NODE_DATA(nid)->zonelist even if NODE_DATA(nid)=3D=3DNULL
   =20
    Then, what's we need is making policy->mems_allowed be aware of
    N_HIGH_MEMORY.  This patch does that.  But to do so, extra nodemask w=
ill
    be on statck.  Because I know cpumask has a new interface of
    CPUMASK_ALLOC(), I added it to node.
   =20
    This patch stands on old behavior.  But I feel this fix itself is jus=
t a
    Band-Aid.  But to do fundametal fix, we have to take care of memory
    hotplug and it takes time.  (task->mems_allowd should be N_HIGH_MEMOR=
Y, I
    think.)
   =20
    mpol_set_nodemask() should be aware of N_HIGH_MEMORY and policy's nod=
emask
    should be includes only online nodes.
   =20
    In old behavior, this is guaranteed by frequent reference to cpuset's
    code.  Now, most of them are removed and mempolicy has to check it by
    itself.
   =20
    To do check, a few nodemask_t will be used for calculating nodemask. =
 But,
    size of nodemask_t can be big and it's not good to allocate them on s=
tack.
   =20
    Now, cpumask_t has CPUMASK_ALLOC/FREE an easy code for get scratch ar=
ea.
    NODEMASK_ALLOC/FREE shoudl be there.
   =20
