    mfd: twl4030 irq fixes
   =20
    The TWL4030 IRQ handler has a bug which leads to spinlock lock-up. It=
 is
    calling the 'unmask' function in a process context. :The mask/unmask/=
ack
    functions are only designed to be called from the IRQ handler code,
    or the proper API interfaces found in linux/interrupt.h.
   =20
    Also there is no need to have IRQ chaining mechanism. The right way t=
o
    handle this is to claim the parent interrupt as a standard interrupt
    and arrange for handle_twl4030_pih to take care of the rest of the de=
vices.
   =20
    Mail thread on this issue can be found at:
    http://marc.info/?l=3Dlinux-arm-kernel&m=3D124629940123396&w=3D2
   =20
    Signed-off-by: Russell King <rmk+kernel-lFZ/pmaqli7XmaaqVzeoHQ@public.gmane.org>
