    Make pci_claim_resource() use request_resource() rather than insert_r=
esource()
   =20
    This function has traditionally used "insert_resource()", because bef=
ore
    commit cebd78a8c5 ("Fix pci_claim_resource") it used to just insert t=
he
    resource into whatever root resource tree that was indicated by
    "pcibios_select_root()".
   =20
    So there Matthew fixed it to actually look up the proper parent
    resource, which means that now it's actively wrong to then traverse t=
he
    resource tree any more: we already know exactly where the new resourc=
e
    should go.
   =20
    And when we then did commit a76117dfd6 ("x86: Use pci_claim_resource"=
),
    which changed the x86 PCI code from the open-coded
   =20
    	pr =3D pci_find_parent_resource(dev, r);
    	if (!pr || request_resource(pr, r) < 0) {
   =20
    to using
   =20
    	if (pci_claim_resource(dev, idx) < 0) {
   =20
    that "insert_resource()" now suddenly became a problem, and causes a
    regression covered by
   =20
    	http://bugzilla.kernel.org/show_bug.cgi?id=3D13891
   =20
    which this fixes.
   =20
