commit e4c6f8bed01f9f9a5c607bd689bf67e7b8a36bd8
Author: Eric Sandeen <sandeen-+82itfer+wXR7s880joybQ@public.gmane.org>
Date:   Wed Jul 29 15:02:16 2009 -0700

    hugetlbfs: fix i_blocks accounting
   =20
    As reported in Red Hat bz #509671, i_blocks for files on hugetlbfs ge=
t
    accounting wrong when doing something like:
   =20
       $ > foo
       $ date  > foo
       date: write error: Invalid argument
       $ /usr/bin/stat foo
         File: `foo'
         Size: 0          Blocks: 18446744073709547520 IO Block: 2097152 =
regular
    ...
   =20
    This is because hugetlb_unreserve_pages() is unconditionally removing
    blocks_per_huge_page(h) on each call rather than using the freed amou=
nt.
    If there were 0 blocks, it goes negative, resulting in the above.
   =20
    This is a regression from commit a5516438959d90b071ff0a484ce4f3f523dc=
3152
    ("hugetlb: modular state for hugetlb page size")
   =20
    which did:
   =20
    -	inode->i_blocks -=3D BLOCKS_PER_HUGEPAGE * freed;
    +	inode->i_blocks -=3D blocks_per_huge_page(h);
   =20
    so just put back the freed multiplier, and it's all happy again.
   =20
