    page-allocator: preserve PFN ordering when __GFP_COLD is set
   =20
    Fix a post-2.6.24 performace regression caused by
    3dfa5721f12c3d5a441448086bee156887daa961 ("page-allocator: preserve P=
FN
    ordering when __GFP_COLD is set").
   =20
    Narayanan reports "The regression is around 15%.  There is no disk co=
ntroller
    as our setup is based on Samsung OneNAND used as a memory mapped devi=
ce on a
    OMAP2430 based board."
   =20
    The page allocator tries to preserve contiguous PFN ordering when ret=
urning
    pages such that repeated callers to the allocator have a strong chanc=
e of
    getting physically contiguous pages, particularly when external fragm=
entation
    is low.  However, of the bulk of the allocations have __GFP_COLD set =
as they
    are due to aio_read() for example, then the PFNs are in reverse PFN o=
rder.
    This can cause performance degration when used with IO controllers th=
at could
    have merged the requests.
   =20
    This patch attempts to preserve the contiguous ordering of PFNs for u=
sers of
    __GFP_COLD.
   =20
