    controller driver.  The xHC will return an error code when the error =
count
    transitions from 1 to 0.  Programming an error count of 3 means the x=
HC tries
    the transfer 3 times, programming it with a 1 means it tries to trans=
fer once,
    and programming it with 0 means the HW tries the transfer infinitely.
   =20
    We want isochronous transfers to only be tried once, so set the error=
 count to
    one.
   =20
