Author: Alan Cox <alan-VuQAYsv1563Yd54FQh9/CA@public.gmane.org>
Date:   Thu Jul 16 16:07:03 2009 +0100

    n_tty: Fix echo race
   =20
    If a tty in N_TTY mode with echo enabled manages to get itself into a=
 state
    where
    	- echo characters are pending
    	- FASYNC is enabled
    	- tty_write_wakeup is called from either
    		- a device write path (pty)
    		- an IRQ (serial)
   =20
    then it either deadlocks or explodes taking a mutex in the IRQ path.
   =20
    On the serial side it is almost impossible to reproduce because you h=
ave to
    go from a full serial port to a near empty one with echo characters
    pending. The pty case happens to have become possible to trigger usin=
g
    emacs and ptys, the pty changes having created a scenario which shows=
 up
    this bug.
   =20
    The code path is
   =20
    	n_tty:process_echoes() (takes mutex)
    	tty_io:tty_put_char()
    	pty:pty_write  (or serial paths)
    	tty_wakeup     (from pty_write or serial IRQ)
    	n_tty_write_wakeup()
    	process_echoes()
    	*KABOOM*
   =20
    Signed-off-by: Alan Cox <alan-VuQAYsv1563Yd54FQh9/CA@public.gmane.org>
    Signed-off-by: Linus Torvalds <torvalds-de/tnXTf+JLsfHDXvbKv3WD2FQJk+8+b@public.gmane.org>

