   =20
    See http://gcc.gnu.org/onlinedocs/gcc-4.1.2/gcc/Optimize-Options.html
   =20
    An example that clearly shows this 'problem' is commit 6bf67672.
   =20
     static void __devexit agnx_pci_remove(struct pci_dev *pdev)
     {
         struct ieee80211_hw *dev =3D pci_get_drvdata(pdev);
    -    struct agnx_priv *priv =3D dev->priv;
    +    struct agnx_priv *priv;
         AGNX_TRACE;
   =20
         if (!dev)
             return;
    +    priv =3D dev->priv;
   =20
    By reverting this patch, and compile it with and without
    -fno-delete-null-pointer-checks flag, we can see that the check for d=
ev
    is compiled away.
   =20
        call    printk  #
    -   testq   %r12, %r12  # dev
    -   je  .L94    #,
        movq    %r12, %rdi  # dev,
   =20
    Clearly the 'fix' is to stop using dev before it is tested, but build=
ing
    with -fno-delete-null-pointer-checks flag at least makes it harder to
    abuse.
