    arch/blackfin: Add kmalloc NULL tests
   =20
    Check that the result of kmalloc is not NULL before passing it to oth=
er
    functions.
   =20
    In the first two cases, the new code returns -ENOMEM, which seems
    compatible with what is done for similar functions for other architec=
tures.
   =20
    In the last two cases, the new code fails silently, ie just returns,
    because the function has void return type.
   =20
    The semantic match that finds this problem is as follows:
    (http://www.emn.fr/x-info/coccinelle/)
   =20
    // <smpl>
    @@
    expression *x;
    identifier f;
    constant char *C;
    @@
   =20
    x =3D \(kmalloc\|kcalloc\|kzalloc\)(...);
    ... when !=3D x =3D=3D NULL
        when !=3D x !=3D NULL
        when !=3D (x || ...)
    (
    kfree(x)
    |
    f(...,C,...,x,...)
    |
    *f(...,x,...)
    |
    *x->f
    )
    // </smpl>
   =20
    Signed-off-by: Julia Lawall <julia-dAYI7NvHqcQ@public.gmane.org>
